{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542995-curseborne-can-dead-become-permanently-incorporeal","id":1542995,"title":"[Curseborne] Can Dead become permanently incorporeal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-02T01:41:19-07:00","id":1542995,"title":"[Curseborne] Can Dead become permanently incorporeal?","content":"Like normal PCs Dead are like <b>Crow </b>1994 movie - you are haunting your own once living body. But can Dead become like old stories ghosts, haunting particular location, without their proper bodies? \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-02T17:28:11-07:00","id":1543041,"title":"","content":"As far as I could see, having a body (which does not have to be your original body) is what distinguishes the Dead from other ghosts, and keeps them from devolving into mindless incorporeal beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T03:54:42-07:00","id":1543053,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Phantasms is collective name for all 'spiritual beings' in <b>Curseborne</b> ( like 'Ephemera' was in <b>CoD</b> ) - and ghosts are particular type of Phantasms made out of dead humans souls. We will probably see with tommorow chapter on Dead more info about this 'de-evolution' from Dead to ghost Phantasm. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T10:12:46-07:00","id":1543065,"title":"","content":"The section on the Wardens in today's preview mentions that their family head &quot;doesn't have a body anymore.&quot; So maybe powerful Dead can stay incorporeal without losing their minds.<br /> <br /> Then again, the Wardens are pretty clearly a cult, so anything they say about &quot;Mother&quot; should be taken with a grain of salt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T18:00:02-07:00","id":1543073,"title":"","content":"Since I haven't seen anyone mention it, the section on the Dead released today makes it clear that one of the two ways the Dead can completely die* is being divorced from a body too long, so the answer for now is pretty flatly a no. That said, since the core book is covering low-Entanglement characters (capping at 4), we currently don't have anything saying it's off the table for higher level Dead (though I wouldn't count on it, given the predilection of the creators as demosntrated before hand).<br /> <br /> *admittedly the way they frame it is a bit of a stretch, since it's more like becoming a (potentially very powerful) Phantasm, but the framing makes it clear the person you were is not retrievable from this state, so semantics asides, it is still dying.. Word on if <i>something</i> is retrievable from that condition is likely the province of sidebars at best in the Core, but might be explored more in future supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-03T19:47:21-07:00","id":1543078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542995-curseborne-can-dead-become-permanently-incorporeal?p=1543065#post1543065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The section on the Wardens in today's preview mentions that their family head &quot;doesn't have a body anymore.&quot; So maybe powerful Dead can stay incorporeal without losing their minds.<br /> <br /> Then again, the Wardens are pretty clearly a cult, so anything they say about &quot;Mother&quot; should be taken with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal impression so far is that Family Heads, at least the \u201cgreat\u201d ones, don\u2019t really abide to the same rules as PCs, period. They\u2019re as much \u201crandom weird shit\u201d as everything else in the setting.<br /> <br /> Of course, there may be some in-universe explanation, there may be some sense in this, but the main point stands as far as they being something or doing something goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T08:06:41-07:00","id":1544557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1542995-curseborne-can-dead-become-permanently-incorporeal?p=1543073#post1543073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I haven't seen anyone mention it, the section on the Dead released today makes it clear that one of the two ways the Dead can completely die* is being divorced from a body too long, so the answer for now is pretty flatly a no. That said, since the core book is covering low-Entanglement characters (capping at 4), we currently don't have anything saying it's off the table for higher level Dead (though I wouldn't count on it, given the predilection of the creators as demosntrated before hand).<br /> <br /> *admittedly the way they frame it is a bit of a stretch, since it's more like becoming a (potentially very powerful) Phantasm, but the framing makes it clear the person you were is not retrievable from this state, so semantics asides, it is still dying.. Word on if <i>something</i> is retrievable from that condition is likely the province of sidebars at best in the Core, but might be explored more in future supplements.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't count on it either, I do think that there's a decent chance that higher-Entanglement characters might undergo fundamental shifts in their nature akin to how <b>Scion</b>'s Heroes, Demigods, and Gods do. If so, I could see Entanglement 5 Dead being considerably less reliant on their corpses than the core book's Dead are, possibly making the Dead at these levels interact with the physical world in a manner closer to WoD wraiths or CoD ghosts (e.g., with multiple anchors that they can move among and manifest through, and with less need to actually <i>inhabit</i> an anchor). If this theory is correct, then it might also be that Dead with sufficiently high Entanglement (say, 9 or 10) might be able to do without physical anchors altogether, using their Entanglement with the web of curses itself to sustain themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}